# Supercook subagent launch

Full wire format and commands: [.cursor/supercook/subagent-launch.md](../supercook/subagent-launch.md).

Before each launch, run `python3 <repo>/scripts/validate_subagent_launch.py` via the `task` or `create-agent` subcommand (long prompts: `.supercook/prompts/<phase>-<role>.md` plus `task --prompt-file`).

- **task**: `description`, `subagent_type`, and `prompt` only under `arguments`.
- **create-agent**: `description`, `subagent_type`, and `prompt` at the top level, never under `arguments`.

A validator rejection means fix and re-run, never run the role inline. Only when the host rejects an already validated launch after a retry may the parent log `degraded: parent inline` with the exact error and run the role itself. Never silently parent-implement instead of launching the subagent.
